#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# quote

#% text
# `quote(x)` keeps `x` unevaluated and stays as it is when passed on, until `unquote` releases it. `eval(e)` written as the argument is evaluated first.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
quote(1 + 2)
#% output
#= quote(1 + 2)

#% cell
quote(eval(1 + 2))
#% output
#= quote(3)

#% cell
unquote(quote(1 + 2))
#% output
#= 3

#% cell
length(quote(f(1 + 1, 2 + 2)))
#% output
#= 1

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `unquote`, `hold_complete`, `eval`
